# Per-machine direnv environment for a child repo consuming this repo as a
# .standards/ submodule (spec 025).
#
# ONE-TIME SETUP:
#   1. Install direnv (https://direnv.net) and wire the hook once in your
#      shell profile:
#        eval "$(direnv hook bash)"   # or your shell's hook
#   2. This file is written for you by ./.standards/scripts/bootstrap.sh
#      (a copy of templates/.envrc.child). If you created it by hand instead,
#      run `direnv allow` at the child repo root. The child .envrc is
#      PER-MACHINE and gitignored — NEVER commit it.
#
# WHAT EACH LINE LOADS (later lines win: a dotenv line clobbers any
# pre-existing value — the .envrc is the per-directory source of truth):
#   1. .standards/config/model.local.env.example — the PARENT.s committed defaults for
#      the 8 SPEC_*_MODEL vars. The submodule never carries
#      gitignored files, so a parent's per-machine override never propagates;
#      this line always resolves against the committed example only.
#   2. config/model.local.env — this child's gitignored per-machine override.
#   3. config/agent.local.env — this child's gitignored per-machine
#      credentials (GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN).
dotenv_if_exists .standards/config/model.local.env.example
dotenv_if_exists config/model.local.env
dotenv_if_exists config/agent.local.env
